From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0770: NVIDIA DLSS Super Resolution through Streamline as temporal_aa_upscaler=dlss (Direct3D 12)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (DLSS study, $WORK/scratch/dlss/DESIGN.md). The calls are NVIDIA Streamline 2.14.16's
  public API (sl.h, sl_dlss.h; "manual hooking" integration, ProgrammingGuide.md, ProgrammingGuideDLSS.md,
  ProgrammingGuideManualHooking.md); no NVIDIA code is copied: the headers are included from the SDK folder that
  REXGLUE_STREAMLINE_DIR names, outside this tree, and the DLLs are loaded at run time
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause). NVIDIA's
  Streamline SDK and its DLLs are NVIDIA's (their licence.txt) and are never in the tree or the patch: mcla-x86's
  tools/setup.py downloads them into the work folder and the install step copies the DLLs next to the executable
Purpose: temporal_aa_upscaler=dlss runs NVIDIA DLSS Super Resolution (DLSS 4: the transformer models) in FSR's place for
  temporal_aa=fsr on an RTX GPU, with exactly FSR's inputs: the jittered (Halton 2,3; 8 x ratio^2 phases), squeezed scene
  of the motion blur draw (linear HDR before the tone map: colorBuffersHDR, auto exposure), the gathered render-size
  colour and depth (R32, 1 near: depthInverted), the game's per-vehicle motion vectors (R16G16, previous minus current,
  render pixels, unjittered: mvecScale 1/render size, cameraMotionIncluded), the camera cut as reset; output into the
  same texture that is copied back into the scene. NVIDIA's guide asks more than FSR: the squeezed scene's mip bias is
  one level sharper with dlss (log2(render/display) - 1, clamped at -1.875; DLAA takes texture_lod_bias -1) and the
  jitter has at least 32 phases. temporal_aa_upscale picks the mode (1 DLAA, 1.5 Quality, 1.72
  Balanced, 2 Performance, 3 Ultra Performance), dlss_preset the model (default|j|k|l|m), dlss_debug (bits: log, vector
  sign, reset every frame, no matrices, alpha not upscaled). Found by running it: Streamline 2.14 refuses slSetTagForFrame
  without PreferenceFlags::eUseFrameBasedResourceTagging (set); DLSS's alpha upscaling is on (the output's alpha is
  otherwise left undefined, 0.03 ms); the picture matches native 2000p and FSR in colour and detail (the tint seen in some
  runs is the game's own: the same two states appear without DLSS). Measured on an RTX 4060 Laptop at 3200x2000: DLSS costs
  about 4-5 ms of GPU time in every mode (transformer model at the output size), so it is a quality choice (DLAA), not a
  speed-up: native 2000p 8.4 ms, DLAA / Quality / Performance 12.5-13.5 ms, FSR 3.1 at 1.5x 11.4 ms. Streamline: cvars nvidia_streamline (auto|on|off: auto loads it when
  temporal_aa_upscaler or frame_generation is dlss; never with frame_generation=fsr), streamline_log (0-2),
  streamline_project_id. It is initialised in D3D12Provider::Initialize once the device exists (slInit with manual
  hooking, slSetD3DDevice, slIsFeatureSupported per adapter LUID, NVIDIA GPUs only), and the swap chain is made through
  its proxy factory (Streamline must see every Present). Log lines: `Streamline 2.14.16: active (manual hooking, ...);
  DLSS Super Resolution available (DLSS 310.x.y)`, `Temporal AA: DLSS 310.x.y ready for 3200x2000 from 1600x1000
  (Performance, 2.000x; Direct3D 12 through NVIDIA Streamline, preset default)`; temporal_aa_upscaler_active says the
  same. Clean fallback: no DLLs, not NVIDIA, not supported, or a failed evaluation (the frame is left as it was, DLSS
  given up for the session) -> FSR runs, logged once. The camera matrices DLSS wants (Streamline's clip space) are
  computed in TaaCheckDraw from the motion blur draw's constants (TaaCamera grows; its z mapping of the previous frame
  is unverified). cmake: cmake/rexglue_streamline.cmake, REXGLUE_STREAMLINE_DIR (empty: no DLSS, as before),
  REXGLUE_STREAMLINE_VARIANT (development|production DLLs installed next to the SDK's). Needs 0750-0795.
Bucket: REDO
---
